			"notes": "# FriendLink 1.0.0\n\nFriendLink is an experimental Fabric client mod that brings the official friends-based P2P multiplayer flow to Minecraft 26.1.2.\n\n## Highlights\n\n- Added a compact friends UI inspired by the newer Minecraft snapshot flow.\n- Added friend list, incoming/outgoing request management, add friend, accept, decline, cancel, and remove friend actions.\n- Added host and join actions through official signaling and WebRTC transport.\n- Added automatic Chinese / English text selection based on the game language.\n- Added a mod icon.\n- Improved signaling connection reuse and recovery after broken WebSocket connections.\n- Improved hosted presence keepalive so hosting no longer reconnects signaling unnecessarily.\n- Removed unsafe local-connection handling that could cause registry/protocol errors.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Both players should use the same FriendLink version.\n- The host must enter a single-player world and press **Host** before others join.\n- This mod depends on Mojang/Microsoft online services, official friends presence, signaling, TURN auth, and WebRTC.\n- Network quality may affect connection success, especially on restricted or high-latency networks.\n\n## Disclaimer\n\nFriendLink is an unofficial Minecraft mod. It is not approved by, endorsed by, or associated with Mojang Studios or Microsoft."
		}
